### Sign up (creates the household member + credentials)
POST http://localhost:8666/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jane",
  "password": "secret123",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-01",
  "countryOfResidence": "Switzerland",
  "countryOfEmployment": "Switzerland",
  "averageMonthlySalary": 6000.00,
  "currentCash": 15000.00
}

### Sign up with an already-taken username -> 409 Conflict
POST http://localhost:8666/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jane",
  "password": "secret123",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-01",
  "countryOfResidence": "Switzerland",
  "countryOfEmployment": "Switzerland",
  "averageMonthlySalary": 6000.00,
  "currentCash": 15000.00
}

### Wrong Log in -> the client keeps the JSESSIONID cookie for the next requests
POST http://localhost:8666/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jane",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### Coorect Log in -> the client keeps the JSESSIONID cookie for the next requests
POST http://localhost:8666/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alibaba",
  "password": "Reuss1r+"
}

### Log in with the wrong password -> 401 Unauthorized
POST http://localhost:8666/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jane",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### Who am I? (requires the session cookie from the successful login above)
GET http://localhost:8666/api/auth/me

### Household members now require a session too
GET http://localhost:8666/api/household-member

### Without a session at all -> 401 Unauthorized
# Run this in a fresh session (e.g. a new HTTP Client environment, or after Log out below)
GET http://localhost:8666/api/auth/me

### Log out (invalidates the session)
POST http://localhost:8666/api/auth/logout

### After logout, the session is gone -> 401 Unauthorized
GET http://localhost:8666/api/auth/me
